-- A checked definition whose type is Π x1 … xk. l ≡ r is an identity; rule-of reads its type
-- through quote-ty and makes the rule l → r with the bound variables as metavariables; rule-of-sym
-- reads it right to left. pool-hyperfactor anti-unifies repeated subterms across any pool of Code
-- definitions into closed de Bruijn λ-templates regardless of caller variable ordering or binder
-- depth whenever m + K·(1 + 2m) < (K - 1)·|body|, composing hierarchically across rounds.
peel-pi : Code → Opt (Code × Code)
peel-pi (cpi m A B) = peel-pi B
peel-pi (cpathp A l r) = some (l , r)
peel-pi c = none
